WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.300
- Well, speaking of birthdays,

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.710
so "Boys in the Hood," is
it the 30th anniversary?

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:04.543
(crowd cheering and clapping)
- Yes,

00:00:04.543 --> 00:00:05.376
yeah-
- Last summer?

00:00:05.376 --> 00:00:06.209
- Something like that, yeah.

00:00:06.209 --> 00:00:07.218
(crowd cheering and clapping)
(Kelly's voice drowns)

00:00:07.218 --> 00:00:08.051
- I mean,

00:00:09.157 --> 00:00:11.200
the film, it just,

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.452
such a pop culture-
- I was only 10.

00:00:12.452 --> 00:00:13.285
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:13.285 --> 00:00:14.118
So if you do the math,
(Kelly's hands tapping)

00:00:14.118 --> 00:00:14.951
if you do the math,

00:00:14.951 --> 00:00:15.784
it's-
- Yeah.

00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:16.617
Oh heck, God, no!

00:00:16.617 --> 00:00:18.720
But it's, why do you think
people resonated so much then?

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.650
And honestly, unfortunately,
still resonate with it now.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.203
- You know, it's interesting
because first of all,

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.470
shout out to the great,
late great John Singleton,

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:30.560
he was incredible.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.614
He was just a

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:32.447
(crowd cheering and clapping)
great visionary.

00:00:32.447 --> 00:00:33.620
- Yeah.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.520
- But I think a lot of the themes still

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.350
are very prevalent to this day.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.420
- Which kinda sucks.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.260
- It does, yeah, it really does.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.310
And then, he put together,

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:43.840
it was a great script that he wrote,

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.140
he directed a great
movie, and he assembled

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.233
a great cast of people who
were just really good people.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.830
And it's, it was just an
incredible project to be a part of.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.910
- Yeah, I mean, I can imagine,
especially as an actor,

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.170
like, it's cool to be a
part of something that just

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:01.900
hits pop culture in such
a way, but also has such

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:02.970
an important message.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:03.803
- Without a doubt.

00:01:03.803 --> 00:01:07.560
I mean, to think now that people
are still talking about it,

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.950
it's, when I did that movie
so many years ago, I mean,

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.360
I just wanted to be a part of something,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.510
I just wanted to get a job, I
just wanted to be in a movie,

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.050
and there's no way I
thought that it would be,

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.240
people would still be talking
about it to this very day.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.353
So, it's a blessing.

